Z||000000||rnoswal||07-03-2001||09:49 PM||||I was just curious as to which nose piece that came on the various models is better, if any, for cooling. I have an 85 and it cools okay but I like the styles of the later nose pieces. Anyone???<P>Thanks <BR>Russ||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||07-03-2001||10:02 PM||||the cooling comes for the air being deflected up from the lower air dam right below the radiator-If it is still there?||||reg||1
Z||000002||rnoswal||07-03-2001||11:07 PM||||My nose piece is intact. I was just wondering which nose was better on the fiero's, if any one is better than the other. Or is it just merely that they are all the same, but just look different?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||07-03-2001||11:56 PM||||I'd have to say air flow is diferant for each style but it's hard to say just how....<P>My Quick Guess, best to worst, I'd say the late coupe and GT are a toss up... The original I think is probably the worst.<P>Just as important however is what's behind the nose etc... A nose that promotes air ramming isn't much help if there is nothing confining that air to entering the condenser and radiator. The space behind the nose of the fieros I've seen is wide open. that means allot of whatever rammed air is simply diverting out to the wheel wells.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sootah||07-04-2001||02:30 PM||||My buddy has an 86 SE (I think) It had the coupe nose on the front. He changed it to the GT nose and made a little scoop right below the radiator to catch the air going under the car. I'll take pics if I can manage to let Phil or Dave let me borrow their digital camera. Oh, his car runs at about 160 consitantly, even in our 105º weather.<P>------------------<BR>Never argue with an idiot, they drag you down to their level and then beat you with experience||||reg||1
